-        <div class="legend-row">
-          <span class="key"><span class="pill proven">proven</span></span>
-          <span class="txt">Sorry-free on the soundness side. Every proven link of the opening line (rows 1–9) is <b>axiom-clean</b> — only <span class="mono">propext / Classical.choice / Quot.sound</span> — and they compose that way: <span class="mono">iteration</span>, <span class="mono">roundsChain</span> and <span class="mono">finalEvalPackage</span> carry no <span class="mono">sorryAx</span>. The <b>honest-prover / completeness layer</b> is tracked in its own files (the <span class="mono">*/Completeness.lean</span> files, <span class="mono">HonestChain.lean</span>, <span class="mono">Correctness.lean</span> — all sorry-free, with composition inheriting the admitted <span class="mono">append_completeness</span>), so a <span class="mono">proven</span> pill on a spine row means the CWSS certificate, not the forward direction.</span>
-        </div>
-        <div class="legend-row">
-          <span class="key"><span class="pill repaired">repaired</span></span>
-          <span class="txt">Sorry-free, but <b>deliberately not the paper's claim</b>: the printed statement is false or unprovable as written, and what is proved here is a corrected variant. The theorem is real — the divergence is what this pill flags, so it is <em>not</em> counted as <span class="mono">proven</span>. Row&nbsp;6 (Lemma&nbsp;10) is the only one: the uniform-vector extraction is refuted by <span class="mono">exists_nonzero_vanishing_on_axis_cross</span> and replaced by per-coordinate scalar rounds with a nested binary-evaluation-tree zero test, with <span class="mono">liftShort</span> carried at the point seams as the commitment's shortness index, not assumed — it is <em>derived</em> from the range identity <span class="mono">H₀ ≡ 0</span> one link earlier. Each such divergence is recorded in <span class="mono">docs/kb/audits/</span>.</span>
-        </div>
-        <div class="legend-row">
-          <span class="key"><span class="pill wip">wip</span></span>
-          <span class="txt">A real skeleton: types, relations, verifier and package are defined and typecheck; the CWSS proof (and sometimes the encoding defs) are <span class="mono">sorry</span>. It sits in the §4.5 recursion tail (rows&nbsp;10&nbsp;and&nbsp;12), which is <b>currently deferred</b> (recursion is not being pursued for now), plus <span class="mono">Commitment.lean</span>'s single sorry — the <em>recursive</em> <span class="mono">opening</span> placeholder.</span>
-        </div>
-        <div class="legend-row">
-          <span class="key"><span class="pill gap">gap</span></span>
-          <span class="txt">A documented soundness gap: the paper's step is (apparently) not knowledge-sound as stated, so the pull-back <span class="mono">sorry</span> stands as the record — the §4.5/§3.2 partial-evaluation gap in <span class="mono">Recursion/ZBatchBridge.lean</span>. No link on the current line carries it: the adapter holding it is future work, below.</span>
-        </div>
-        <div class="legend-row">
-          <span class="key"><span class="pill plan">planned</span></span>
-          <span class="txt">Named in the composition roadmap but not yet a file — the §3 packing head, the §4.4/§4.5 termination tails, and the knowledge-error accounting. (The completeness layer is no longer among them: it is delivered, in the <span class="mono">*/Completeness.lean</span> files, <span class="mono">HonestChain.lean</span>, <span class="mono">Correctness.lean</span> and <span class="mono">Concrete.lean</span>.)</span>
-        </div>
